# BlueROV2 on ArduSub, loaded after ArduPilot's default_params/sub.parm.
# BiguaSim model: dynamics.marine.MarinePlant, 10.5 kg, six T200 thrusters at -278.9..278.9 rad/s (k_eta w|w|).

# Vectored frame: MOT1..4 horizontal (front-right, front-left, rear-right, rear-left), MOT5 / MOT6 right / left
# vertical. The bridge drives the BiguaSim thrusters with them (signs and order in vehicle.py).
FRAME_CONFIG    1
MOT_PWM_MIN     1100
MOT_PWM_MAX     1900

# One IMU sample per physics step (200 Hz): ArduPilot wants them at 1.8 x its loop rate or more.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 100

# GUIDED / AUTO speed. The BlueROV2 has no pitch control: the horizontal thrust tilts it until the righting moment
# holds it. BiguaSim's own controller allows 0.25 m/s for that tilt to stay under 30 deg (MarinePlant._speed_limit,
# box hull); offline at 0.25 m/s the worst tilt is 22 deg, at 0.5 m/s it tips over to 72 deg.
WP_SPD          0.25
WP_ACC          0.25
